=== PARITY (vs web SentryEventLogWidget.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> bound via the shared state-holder seam (SentrySource -> SentryModel):
    useVehicles, useTranslation, useQuery('/security?vehicle_id=&limit='). The production app wires
    SentrySource by composing the vehicles store (web id = vehicleId ?? vehicles[0].id) with the
    security-events query; the view performs NO HTTP.
  Projection -> SentryEventCatalog.derive is a 1:1 port of the web `deriveEvent` precedence ladder:
    open-doors (amber #f59e0b, warning) > sentry-on (cyan #06b6d4, info) > sentry-off (slate #6b7280,
    info) > locked (green #22c55e, info) > unlocked (red #ef4444, critical) > "security state updated"
    (purple #8b5cf6, info). openDoors() reproduces split(',')→trim→filter(includes 'open'); the door
    title echoes the token list ("Door open: <tokens>"). Subtitle reproduces parts.join(' · ') || '—'
    (🔒 Locked / 🔓 Unlocked + 🛡️ Sentry On / Sentry Off). displayTimestamp = created_at ?? ts;
    stableID = id ?? "<vehicle_id>-<ts>". SentryFeedBuilder sorts newest-first + caps. All verified
    by the EXECUTED XCTest below.
  Layout -> SentryLayout.eventLimit(size) = isWide(cols>=3) ? 10 : isTall(rows>=2) ? 7 : 4, and
    showsSubtitle = cols>=3 (web `isWide`). Default 2×4 → 7 rows, no subtitle. Verified by tests.
  Composition -> shell chrome (shield icon + "Sentry Event Log" title + freshness chip + refresh +
    optional Open) · newest-first event feed (timeline icon in the event color + localized title +
    relative time + lock/sentry subtitle when wide) · feed empty state. SF Symbols: door.left.hand.open
    / eye.fill / eye.slash.fill / lock.fill / lock.open.fill / door.left.hand.closed.
  Shared components -> reuses Color.TS / Font.TS / TSSpacing / TSRadius / TSTone (real Badges.swift) /
    TSSkeleton + ContentUnavailableView, compiled against the REAL design tokens in the typechecks
    below. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map on this surface).
  States (all render) -> loading (skeleton rows) · empty (ContentUnavailableView "No security events
    recorded") · error (retry affordance) · stale (chip + banner) · offline (cached rows + chip +
    banner) · content; PLUS the feed-level empty fallback. Model phase resolution keeps cached rows
    visible behind refresh/errors, matching the web shell.
  i18n -> all source strings resolve through the P1/S10 facade (table "SentryEventLogWidget") with the
    web English fallback; the web `deriveEvent` titles + subtitle fragments are hardcoded literals in
